                "entry_id": "b713760e-8983-3411-bc9b-648b6c48b4a4",
                "word": "genderflux",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a69eb164-0fb3-3e51-adf5-95c0b62d735e",
                        "entry_id": "b713760e-8983-3411-bc9b-648b6c48b4a4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Personne qui se reconnaît dans une identité de genre qui varie en intensité au cours du temps."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Genres humains et identités de genre",
                            "Transitude"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6e305b85-4e7f-4abb-84a6-e31f76763520",
                                "sense_id": "a69eb164-0fb3-3e51-adf5-95c0b62d735e",
                                "text": "Tenter de creuser, de bâtir une réflexion à partir du ressenti, même en tant que la personne qui ressent, devient une sorte de tabou. On se croirait à Poudlard, tiens. Le choixpeau décide, “te voilà genderflux et sapiosexuel-le”, et ces catégories qu’on dirait créées par Dieu sont littéralement indiscutables."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5d82eb32-b6a8-43b1-9784-4ab56fd680c8",
                        "source_entry_id": "b713760e-8983-3411-bc9b-648b6c48b4a4",
                        "source_sense_id": "a69eb164-0fb3-3e51-adf5-95c0b62d735e",
                        "target_lang_word": "genderflux",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "genderflux",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6641c65d-fd1d-39d9-952a-4fbe0ae35cd0",
                                        "entry_id": "5f453c03-3e56-3d0c-84eb-b89df413f6ab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having a gender identity which fluctuates, either in intensity or between multiple genders."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7992b1e3-99e5-4133-b62d-fc8be7c0c0a7",
                                                "sense_id": "6641c65d-fd1d-39d9-952a-4fbe0ae35cd0",
                                                "text": "While I am poly-genderflux (meaning I experience several different genders fluctuating), genderflux to others could just be some days feeling like a boy, and then other days not really having the same vibe. Essentially to me, genderflux ..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "42f4ab1d-657f-464f-9dab-14e0987066fb",
                                                "sense_id": "6641c65d-fd1d-39d9-952a-4fbe0ae35cd0",
                                                "text": "Usually a genderflux person will identify as a man or a woman, on any given day. […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fed01526-7e79-4023-8972-5161ee6a33fe",
                                                "sense_id": "6641c65d-fd1d-39d9-952a-4fbe0ae35cd0",
                                                "text": "(e.g. biflux, a genderflux identity with two specific gender aspects, or demigirl, […] )"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce23426c-1e1a-4eee-bef2-4ad279c2dc51",
                                                "sense_id": "6641c65d-fd1d-39d9-952a-4fbe0ae35cd0",
                                                "text": "“How do you describe yourself?” I asked. “Genderflux femme,” Cori said. “What's genderflux?” I asked. “Genderflux femme means I'm more and less femme. I'm fluxing ...\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4bfa6873-5487-4c3f-ac98-6964c1ea9c96",
                                                "sense_id": "6641c65d-fd1d-39d9-952a-4fbe0ae35cd0",
                                                "text": "This latter group includes, but is not limited to, those who experience not having a gender identity (agender) or as having a gender identity that is changing and shifting over time (genderfluid or genderflux)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
